    <active>true</active>
    <entityName>Lead</entityName>
    <fieldName>Status</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>Sales Lead Path</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_Status__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_State__c</fieldNames>
        <picklistValueName>Contact - No Opportunity</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_Status__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_Sub_Status__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_State__c</fieldNames>
        <info>&lt;p&gt;Overview: In the MQL stage, assess a lead&amp;#39;s suitability for sales pursuit. Gather PACTT info and confirm project start timing within 6 months.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actions:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1. Check if account is covered; reference it in &amp;#39;Business Information&amp;#39;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. Contact the person and log activity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. After talking with the customer, change Sub Status to &amp;#39;In Contact&amp;#39;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4. If lead is not worth pursuing, mark status &amp;#39;Disqualified&amp;#39; with reason.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;5. If lead has potential, keep logging activities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;6. If start date exceeds 6 months or lead is not PACTT qualified, mark status &amp;#39;Disqualified&amp;#39; with reason.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;7. If lead has purchase propensity, change Status to &amp;#39;Qualified&amp;#39;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;8. If you are a BDR, contact Sales Rep; if they want to pursue, reassign lead.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;9. If Sales Rep does not accept lead, mark status &amp;#39;Disqualified&amp;#39; with &amp;#39;Not accepted by Sales&amp;#39;.&lt;/p&gt;</info>
        <picklistValueName>Marketing Qualified Lead</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_Status__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_Sub_Status__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_State__c</fieldNames>
        <info>&lt;p&gt;Overview: In the SAL stage a Sales Rep has accepted the qualified Lead with PACTT information. The Sales Rep continues to validate the Lead and if there is a high level to purchase an Intel Product/Solution, convert the Lead to on opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actions:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1. Attempt to establish contact with the lead.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. Determine if the lead is an ideal fit and project is ready for opportunity pursuit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. If so, mark SAL stage as complete in the status bar, there by converting the lead to an opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4. If lead is unfit after contact is established , change lead status to &amp;quot;Disqualified&amp;quot; and provide relevant sub-status.&lt;/p&gt;</info>
        <picklistValueName>Sales Accepted Lead</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_Status__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Core_Lead_State__c</fieldNames>
        <picklistValueName>Sales Qualified Lead</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>Lead</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
